# Netlify _redirects — Carmit Therapy Site

# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Domain canonicalisation — consolidate all SEO authority on
# https://carmit-therapy.com (no www, HTTPS only).
# ---------------------------------------------------------------
https://carmit-therapy.netlify.app/*   https://carmit-therapy.com/:splat   301!
http://carmit-therapy.com/*            https://carmit-therapy.com/:splat   301!
http://www.carmit-therapy.com/*        https://carmit-therapy.com/:splat   301!
https://www.carmit-therapy.com/*       https://carmit-therapy.com/:splat   301!

# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# Keep internal project files out of the public site.
# They sit next to the pages, so Netlify publishes them: every one of
# these was reachable (and indexable) at its plain URL.
#
# TWO Netlify gotchas are handled here:
#   1. `*` is only supported as a TRAILING splat, so `/*.md` never matches.
#      Each file is listed explicitly.
#   2. A redirect loses to a real file at the same path unless it is forced
#      with `!`. These are real files, so without the `!` the rules were
#      silently skipped and the documents stayed reachable.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------
/AGENT_CONTEXT.md                     /404.html                                  404!
/SEO_AUDIT.md                         /404.html                                  404!
/SEO_FINAL_VALIDATION.md              /404.html                                  404!
/SEARCH_CONSOLE_CHECKLIST.md          /404.html                                  404!
/.claude/*                            /404.html                                  404!

# ---------------------------------------------------------------
# One canonical address per page.
#
# Netlify used to publish every page under an extensionless URL as
# well, so each page answered on two addresses while the canonical
# tag and the sitemap named only the .html one. Pretty URLs are now
# off (see netlify.toml) and these rules fold the extensionless form
# — including anything Google already crawled — back onto the
# canonical address. They double as friendly short links to hand out
# over the phone or on WhatsApp.
#
# The `!` is required: Netlify resolves /privacy to privacy.html on its
# own, and an unforced redirect always loses to a file it can resolve.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------
/accessibility                        /accessibility.html                        301!
/privacy                              /privacy.html                              301!
/terms                                /terms.html                                301!
/therapy-children-petah-tikva         /therapy-children-petah-tikva.html         301!
/psychotherapist-children-petah-tikva /psychotherapist-children-petah-tikva.html 301!
/cbt-children-petah-tikva             /cbt-children-petah-tikva.html             301!
/נגישות                               /accessibility.html                        301!
# (/index.html is folded onto / by Netlify itself — adding a rule for it
#  here risks a loop, so it is deliberately left out.)
